(264,'PLO 1','Apply fundamental principles of physics, mathematics, computation, and interdisciplinary knowledge to analyze and solve complex problems guided by ethical decision-making. This includes: a. Yielding advanced models from materials science and physics to innovate the design, predict the behavior, and thoroughly characterize novel materials at various scales. b. Integrating core concepts from biological sciences and physics to critically inform the design, development, and optimization of medical instruments and devices. c. Leveraging advanced physical principles and computational methods to model, analyze, and interpret sophisticated economic and financial systems.'),
(264,'PLO 2','Critically evaluate scientific, technical, and economic information from varied sources to design and innovate relevant applications benefiting Philippine society. This includes:a. Utilizing advanced characterization techniques and computational tools to predict, validate, and optimize the performance of designed materials for targeted applications. a. Utilizing advanced characterization techniques and computational tools to predict, validate, and optimize the performance of designed materials for targeted applications. b. Applying specialized knowledge of medical imaging, biomaterials, and other advanced materials to select, integrate, and optimize components for functional devices. c. Drawing informed, interdisciplinary conclusions from scientific literature and economic/financial reports.'),
(264,'PLO 3','Synthesize and communicate complex scientific information and arguments effectively in both oral and written forms to diverse audiences in a logical, clear, and precise manner.'),
